    C0 (length 3): 1(H=3,NS) → 0(H=1,SC) → 2(H=5,NS)
    C1 (length 3): 2(H=5,NS) → 0(H=1,SC) → 3(H=3,SC)
    C2 (length 3): 2(H=5,NS) → 0(H=1,SC) → 4(H=9,SC)
    C3 (length 4): 2(H=5,NS) → 0(H=1,SC) → 1(H=3,NS) → 5(H=9,SC)
    C4 (length 4): 4(H=9,SC) → 0(H=1,SC) → 1(H=3,NS) → 5(H=9,SC)
    C5 (length 4): 4(H=9,SC) → 0(H=1,SC) → 2(H=5,NS) → 6(H=11,SC)
    C6 (length 4): 4(H=9,SC) → 0(H=1,SC) → 3(H=3,SC) → 7(H=15,SC)
    C7 (length 5): 5(H=9,SC) → 1(H=3,NS) → 0(H=1,SC) → 2(H=5,NS) → 6(H=11,SC)
    C8 (length 5): 5(H=9,SC) → 1(H=3,NS) → 0(H=1,SC) → 2(H=5,NS) → 8(H=13,SC)
    C9 (length 3): 6(H=11,SC) → 2(H=5,NS) → 8(H=13,SC)
    C10 (length 5): 7(H=15,SC) → 3(H=3,SC) → 0(H=1,SC) → 2(H=5,NS) → 8(H=13,SC)
    C11 (length 4): 8(H=13,SC) → 2(H=5,NS) → 6(H=11,SC) → 9(H=15,SC)

  TESTING WHICH CYCLES ARE BOUNDARIES:
    C0: BOUNDARY (residual=1.18e-15)
    C1: BOUNDARY (residual=1.61e-15)
    C2: BOUNDARY (residual=1.68e-15)
    C3: BOUNDARY (residual=1.48e-15)
    C4: BOUNDARY (residual=2.79e-15)
    C5: BOUNDARY (residual=2.84e-15)
